WEBVTT

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.480
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.650
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.900
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:34.050
Scattering Beans With Everyone!

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:38.030
Is everyone here?

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:40.550
Thank you very much 
for the invitation.

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:42.390
This is very exciting.

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:45.320
So exciting...

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:47.870
It'll probably be great 
for relieving stress.

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:50.590
Is everything ready, Miss Sasako?

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:52.760
Yes, it is.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:55.420
They're so serious.

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:58.630
Polar Bear is totally 
ready to do this.

00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:01.690
All right, here you go.

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:03.100
Well, we only scatter 
beans once a  year.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:03.100
There.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:07.060
All right. Who's going 
to be the ogre?

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:09.020
Me!

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:11.790
What? You're going to do it, Panda?

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:15.510
Being the ogre sounds super awesome!

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:20.660
I'm all set.

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:23.200
Let's begin scattering the beans.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:25.160
Here I go!

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:28.620
Ogres outside!

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.310
Outside! Outside!

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:30.870
Outside.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:35.340
That hurts.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:38.720
Couldn't you throw a little softer?

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:42.670
Hey! I never heard of 
an ogre complaining!

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:44.810
But it hurts.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.550
We'll throw it a little softer, then.

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:50.900
Ogres outside!

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:51.620
Outside!

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:56.230
I think it still hurts.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.980
It's still too hard?

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:01.160
We're throwing it really softly.

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:04.160
Then we'll do one bean at a time.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:06.120
Ogres...

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:07.670
Outside.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:12.290
I don't think that's scattering beans.

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:14.200
That's more like planting seeds.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:15.290
Give me some beans.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.760
I'll do it myself.

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:21.870
I've never heard of a case where 
the ogre throws beans at itself.

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:25.370
But there could be.

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:29.260
Ogres outside.

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:35.860
Well, this is no fun.

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:39.110
We should get someone that 
looks more like an ogre.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:46.530
Yeah, he does look like 
an ogre to begin with.

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:49.010
You don't even need a mask.

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:51.710
Well, I guess it's you, Mandrill.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:55.730
But I was the ogre last year, too...

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:57.020
Now that you mention it...

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:58.420
Sorry about that.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:03:59.250
And so,

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:02.180
I'll do my best to eat 
the beans this year.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:05.720
It's a little early for that.

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:09.160
Then I'll do it.

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:10.320
Go ahead and throw.

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:12.020
Ogres outsi—

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:12.930
Hey, guys!

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:17.610
Do you all know why we scatter beans?

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:22.570
Um... wasn't it so we can 
expel negative energy?

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:24.090
Precisely!

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:26.980
The changing of the seasons
brings in negative energy.

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:29.070
We scatter beans to extinguish it.

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:31.830
Then we wish for a healthy rest of the year.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:34.750
The reason we use beans

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:37.750
is because they get rid of evil.

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:41.450
And, old-timer, 
the beans that you use

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:43.490
have to be roasted beans.

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:44.910
If you use raw soy beans,

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:46.970
and they are left on the ground, 
they may start sprout—

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:48.470
That's enough!

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:50.930
And you started to do comedic 
storytelling while you were talking!

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:54.190
The kids are completely bored now!

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:56.250
All aboard!

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:57.850
Aboard!

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:03.220
I guess I don't have a choice.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.070
Okay, let's start.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:09.120
Ogres outside!

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.910
Ogres outside!

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:11.870
Hold on one second!

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:14.650
You, go by yourself.

00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:17.140
Me?

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:17.880
Yeah.

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:20.670
Ogres outside!

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:25.010
No, the part after "ogres." 
You're supposed to stretch it out longer.

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:29.680
O-Ogres... outside...

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:30.990
Yeah, like that.

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:34.040
You're too picky, Mr. Penguin.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:36.480
But yelling that is important.

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:39.230
All right, one more time!

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:42.110
Ogres outs—

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:46.190
Hold it, hold it!

00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:49.320
Mr. Llama and Tortoise, 
you guys need to participate, too!

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:51.910
I can't throw, so...

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:56.500
Nor... can... I...

00:05:57.570 --> 00:05:59.780
Everyone has to participate!

00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:02.420
Can't you think of some way to throw?

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:09.130
I-I can do it from my mouth.

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:14.010
Then... I can do it... from my nose...

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:17.730
Let's just accept their 
will to participate.

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:23.230
All right, let's rehearse 
this one more time.

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:27.510
Take your stance... and then throw!

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:30.320
Ogres outside!

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:32.280
Hold it right there!

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:36.950
Miss Sasako, with a 
little more feeling!

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:39.360
Panda, you're completely missing!

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:42.250
Don't throw from so 
high up, Polar Bear.

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:46.180
All right, remember 
the parts I coached you on.

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:47.670
Let's get this started!

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:52.680
Why is no one throwing?

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:56.540
We're done with you as the ogre.

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:58.600
The ogre is being too demanding.

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:01.020
Time to change ogres.

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:06.230
Outside!

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:07.230
Outside.

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:08.100
Outside!

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:08.710
Outside.

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:11.070
But I'm not the ogre anymore.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:11.840
Outside!

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:12.600
Outside.

00:07:14.570 --> 00:07:17.080
Please, hit me with the beans.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:20.960
Mr. Llama's ogre looks really kind.

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:23.260
It's a little hard to hit him.

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:24.290
Indeed.

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:28.010
But I'm the ogre right now. 
So, please, don't hold back.

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:29.530
Then...

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:32.890
Ogres outside!

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:37.120
Ogres outside!

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:41.230
All right, I think it's about time.

00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:46.520
Is it all right if the ogre 
excuses himself outside?

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:50.350
This doesn't feel like 
bean scattering.

00:07:50.350 --> 00:07:52.040
Yeah, something's not right.

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:54.240
He's almost like a butler.

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:56.800
Well, who's next?

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:01.660
Ogres outside!

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:06.590
Just keep on hitting me...

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:10.050
It doesn't hurt at all...

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:13.510
It's true that we don't have 
to hold back at all...

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:16.050
But all the beans are being repelled.

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:19.090
See-saw, see-saw!

00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:19.970
Saw...

00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:22.660
See-saw, see-saw!

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:23.230
See-saw...

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:23.940
Looks like we're having 
trouble finding an ogre...

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:27.060
Then it's up to me again.

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:29.030
No, we've had enough of you.

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:31.050
Then who should be it?

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:36.990
Roar!

00:08:38.570 --> 00:08:41.120
Are you trying
 to be a red ogre?

00:08:42.090 --> 00:08:43.130
Yes...

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:46.000
I'll be the ogre.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.410
Oh, go right ahead.

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:53.010
Are there any crybabies around?!

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:56.970
That's a Namahage...

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:58.470
That's not an ogre.

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:00.930
Ogre <i>(oni)</i>?

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:03.690
Crab <i>(kani)</i>!

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:06.570
Alligator <i>(wani)</i>!

00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:09.900
Sea urchin <i>(uni)</i>!

00:09:10.310 --> 00:09:12.680
Are there any crybabies around?!

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:14.320
Could you please just 
do this seriously?

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:18.290
Isn't there anyone else who's 
like an ogre, Mr. Polar Bear?

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:28.050
So cool!

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.690
He fits the ogre image perfectly.

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:34.010
And his eyes are all red, too.

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:37.190
That's because I haven't 
gotten enough sleep.

00:09:37.190 --> 00:09:38.930
I'm in the middle of hibernating.

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:41.490
Okay, let's start.

00:09:41.490 --> 00:09:43.640
Yeah, let's get this over with.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.080
I'm scared!

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:53.780
No!

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:56.490
Are you all right, Mr. Llama?!

00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:00.620
S-Sorry about that. 
I guess that was too effective.

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:02.850
I'll hold back a little more.

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:08.670
All right, I'm an ogre. 
Throw beans at me!

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:12.520
Ogres outside!

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:16.760
Ogres outside!

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:16.760
Outside!

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:20.300
I-I've been defeated!

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:23.220
I give up!

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:25.560
I've had enough!

00:10:26.650 --> 00:10:29.300
Luck inside!

00:10:31.740 --> 00:10:33.230
That was fun.

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:33.980
Yes.

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:37.950
Thank goodness Mr. Grizzly came.

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:40.200
Are you done now?

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:41.870
Then I'm going home.

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:45.400
Since you came,  
please have some beans.

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:49.200
Yeah. All of us have to 
eat our age in beans.

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:53.360
You get tired of them 
after eating a lot.

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:56.050
Here you go, some other bean dishes.

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:01.140
Bean pilaf, minced meat with beans wrapped in lettuce.

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:03.810
There's some chili con carne, too.

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:05.530
That looks great.

00:11:06.710 --> 00:11:08.620
There's some ehomaki, too.

00:11:09.590 --> 00:11:10.780
Bamboo grass!

00:11:10.780 --> 00:11:11.810
Fish!

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:13.550
...ish!

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:21.780
Finally... eighty...

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:25.220
That looks rough, Mr. Tortoise.

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:33.920
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:11:30.630 --> 00:11:32.650
The Café in the Afternoon!

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:55.950
All right, please look after 
the Café, Miss Sasako.

00:11:57.670 --> 00:11:59.680
Right. See you later.

00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:03.570
Now, then.

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:06.380
I guess I should wipe some glasses.

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:39.860
Reunion Invitation
City Elementary School #1 
35th graduating class's reunion:
1. I will attend.
2. I will not attend.
Venue: Sincerity Home
Date & Time: March 21 at 6PM
Looking forward to reuniting 
with everyone again.

00:12:37.510 --> 00:12:39.290
A reunion, huh?

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:43.610
I haven't been back in a while...

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:49.510
1. I will attend.
2. I will not attend.

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:51.450
Welcome!

00:12:52.110 --> 00:12:53.630
Oh, Mr. Llama.

00:12:54.050 --> 00:12:55.020
Hello.

00:12:58.560 --> 00:12:59.380
Here you go.

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:01.300
Are you ready to order?

00:13:01.910 --> 00:13:04.680
Could I get a coffee, please? 
A cup of Mocha Matari.

00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:05.790
Sure.

00:13:08.960 --> 00:13:11.260
Am I the only customer?

00:13:11.690 --> 00:13:12.350
Yes.

00:13:13.420 --> 00:13:16.030
Are you off from the zoo today?

00:13:16.030 --> 00:13:17.180
Yes.

00:13:17.180 --> 00:13:18.270
I see.

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:25.250
Such a wonderful aroma.

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:31.210
Oh.

00:13:31.210 --> 00:13:32.120
What is it?

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:38.350
This elementary school is right 
by where I used to live.

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:40.090
Oh, really?

00:13:41.070 --> 00:13:43.590
A reunion?

00:13:44.860 --> 00:13:45.550
Indeed.

00:13:46.310 --> 00:13:49.730
So you attended that elementary 
school, Miss Sasako?

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:50.700
I did.

00:13:51.370 --> 00:13:57.000
So does that mean you and I lived in 
the same city before, Mr. Llama?

00:13:58.050 --> 00:13:59.430
That's amazing.

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:02.690
That's a very interesting coincidence.

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:04.190
Then do you know about this?

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:08.280
If you cross at the light at 
the school and continue on,

00:14:09.710 --> 00:14:12.080
there's a bakery if you walk 
a little further down.

00:14:12.670 --> 00:14:14.120
The Asunaro Bakery?

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:16.290
Yes! The Asunaro Bakery.

00:14:17.240 --> 00:14:18.750
The cream bread is delicious.

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:22.220
Yes. The leaf-shaped cream bread.

00:14:23.330 --> 00:14:25.600
There's so much pastry cream in it.

00:14:25.600 --> 00:14:28.220
I loved those.

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:29.530
As did I.

00:14:29.530 --> 00:14:32.720
And then, if you turn right 
at the Asunaro Bakery,

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:36.180
and go a little past 
Mr. Giraffe's house...

00:14:37.110 --> 00:14:38.480
There's Suginoko Park.

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:39.260
Yes!

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:41.480
I played there quite a bit.

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:42.680
So did I.

00:14:44.440 --> 00:14:47.320
Oh, and the person 
who was always cleaning it...

00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:48.900
Mr. Raccoon?

00:14:49.190 --> 00:14:49.860
Yes!

00:14:50.510 --> 00:14:54.230
He always got angry when you didn't 
throw trash away properly.

00:14:54.230 --> 00:14:56.940
He got mad even if you did.

00:14:56.940 --> 00:14:58.330
He'd say that you weren't 
throwing it away right.

00:14:58.900 --> 00:15:01.080
One time when he got angry with me,

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:03.040
I sneakily stuck my tongue out at him,

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:07.100
and then he made me help him 
wash for three hours.

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:09.930
You did that?

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:13.010
I was tad mischievous then.

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:14.890
I see.

00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:15.970
Yes.

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:20.190
Oh, no! 
I forgot to bring out your coffee!

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:23.650
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:15:24.670 --> 00:15:25.620
Here you go.

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:30.680
It's delicious.

00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:32.440
Thank you very much.

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:38.200
So, where was your house in 
relation to Suginoko Park?

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:41.300
You know the bathhouse diagonally 
opposite the park?

00:15:42.820 --> 00:15:44.680
Oh, the Hama no Yu Bathhouse?

00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:45.330
Right!

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:47.630
My house was just on the other side.

00:15:47.870 --> 00:15:50.210
Ah, by Hama no Yu.

00:15:50.560 --> 00:15:53.310
And for some reason, 
there was a small statue

00:15:53.310 --> 00:15:55.350
of a frog holding a bucket out front.

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:57.740
Oh, that's right, the frog!

00:15:57.740 --> 00:15:59.060
And he had a towel on top of his head.

00:15:59.510 --> 00:16:02.460
They said that if you faced backwards 
and tossed a 100 yen coin in,

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:04.950
that something good 
would happen, but...

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:09.840
I'm sure the owner of the bathhouse 
was just saying that.

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:11.460
Of course.

00:16:15.050 --> 00:16:16.910
This is all so nostalgic.

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:19.010
Indeed.

00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:24.110
I had totally forgotten about the 
frog in front of Hama no Yu.

00:16:24.930 --> 00:16:29.040
Oh, why don't you have a 
seat, as well, Miss Sasako?

00:16:31.710 --> 00:16:33.140
You're right.

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:35.340
There aren't any customers, 
so it won't hurt.

00:16:36.290 --> 00:16:38.560
Thank you.

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:42.880
Were you able to get it?

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:43.540
Yeah.

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:45.330
Why did we have to tag along, too?

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:48.610
Because it's hard work collecting dues

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:50.730
for the neighborhood association.

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:53.030
I'm tired.

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:55.390
Then let's take a little break.

00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:57.200
What about the café?

00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:00.660
I've left Miss Sasako in charge.

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:03.150
I see.

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:07.020
So, you lived right behind Hama no Yu?

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:10.520
Then I've probably passed it before.

00:17:11.450 --> 00:17:13.530
It's the house with the fig tree,

00:17:13.530 --> 00:17:17.390
though it was chopped down when 
I was in elementary school.

00:17:17.780 --> 00:17:18.970
I see.

00:17:19.610 --> 00:17:21.060
I don't think I remember it.

00:17:21.780 --> 00:17:24.520
I was in preschool when 
I lived in that city.

00:17:24.860 --> 00:17:29.730
Wait, if you were in preschool 
when I was in elementary school,

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:32.160
does that mean that you're 
younger than me, Mr. Llama?

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:34.530
Oh, I could be.

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:37.260
Oh, I see...

00:17:37.260 --> 00:17:39.410
So, you're younger than me.

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:44.000
Oh, don't worry, Miss Sasako. 
You look much younger than I do.

00:17:44.740 --> 00:17:47.030
Then since we lived in the same city,

00:17:47.030 --> 00:17:49.580
you know about the 
festival at the Megamo Shrine?

00:17:51.400 --> 00:17:52.570
The duck dance!

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:54.170
Duck Dance

00:17:54.520 --> 00:17:56.540
That's right! The duck dance!

00:17:56.540 --> 00:17:58.000
The duck dance.

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:01.410
Oh, that's right.

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:04.980
Do you remember there being 
a large windmill in the west?

00:18:05.720 --> 00:18:06.800
A windmill?

00:18:07.800 --> 00:18:08.810
Oh.

00:18:10.220 --> 00:18:13.430
When I was in second grade, 
during summer vacation,

00:18:13.430 --> 00:18:16.820
I was determined to 
get to that windmill.

00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:23.850
I thought there would be a lot of wind by that giant windmill...

00:18:23.850 --> 00:18:26.000
Enough for me to fly.

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:29.460
I put my water bottle

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:32.130
and Asunaro Bakery's 
cream bread in my backpack

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:34.420
and started walking.

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:43.010
But no matter how much I walked, 
the windmill didn't get any closer.

00:18:45.710 --> 00:18:47.750
The sun started to set,

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:50.940
my cream bread got smushed,

00:18:55.060 --> 00:18:57.400
and the water in my 
water bottle ran out.

00:19:03.790 --> 00:19:06.470
But I still wanted to get 
there, no matter what.

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:09.700
I wanted to fly.

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:19.930
I apparently caused a commotion at 
my house in the meanwhile, though.

00:19:20.310 --> 00:19:21.050
Oh!

00:19:21.820 --> 00:19:23.620
I remember something like that!

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:26.090
I remember hearing that an 
elementary school girl got lost.

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:30.300
So that little girl was 
you, Miss Sasako?

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:31.990
Probably.

00:19:32.620 --> 00:19:36.560
I kept wondering what happened to her.

00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:40.240
So, you made it home safely.

00:19:40.710 --> 00:19:42.660
I'm sorry for the trouble I caused.

00:19:43.270 --> 00:19:44.600
I'm relieved.

00:19:44.600 --> 00:19:49.750
That girl has grown up, 
and is working very hard.

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:54.930
I tried several more times
 to find my way to the windmill,

00:19:54.930 --> 00:19:57.610
but I never did make it.

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:01.200
We're back.

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:03.260
Welcome back.

00:20:03.940 --> 00:20:07.610
Huh? There's no one here.

00:20:07.610 --> 00:20:09.570
Mr. Llama is right there.

00:20:09.570 --> 00:20:11.840
Oh, you're right.

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:12.940
Hello.

00:20:13.780 --> 00:20:15.420
I'm beat.

00:20:15.420 --> 00:20:18.320
I never get tired at my part-time job.

00:20:18.320 --> 00:20:21.650
That's because all you 
do is lay around.

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:23.590
You should actually try 
working harder, you know?

00:20:23.590 --> 00:20:25.470
Thanks to you, we were able to collect

00:20:25.470 --> 00:20:27.270
all the dues for the 
neighborhood association.

00:20:27.270 --> 00:20:28.880
Thank you for all of your hard work.

00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:31.150
Oh, welcome.

00:20:31.150 --> 00:20:32.960
One steamed milk.

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:33.590
Coming right up.

00:20:34.050 --> 00:20:35.390
Hello.

00:20:34.690 --> 00:20:35.390
Hello.

00:20:35.390 --> 00:20:36.540
Welcome.

00:20:37.060 --> 00:20:38.740
Could we take the table near the back?

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:40.430
Sure, go right ahead.

00:20:39.790 --> 00:20:41.630
So, as I was saying earlier...

00:20:43.850 --> 00:20:46.580
A New York cheesecake 
and an apple pie,

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:48.510
then one house blend coffee 
and an Earl Grey tea.

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:50.430
We'll have that out shortly.

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:51.900
Thank you.

00:20:53.180 --> 00:20:55.800
Oh, Mr. Llama, are you heading out?

00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:56.440
Yes.

00:20:56.910 --> 00:20:58.430
Thank you very much.

00:20:58.900 --> 00:20:59.940
I'll come again.

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:00.690
Yes.

00:21:01.680 --> 00:21:06.220
Oh, Miss Sasako, 
I've gone before, too.

00:21:07.130 --> 00:21:08.970
But I was with my father.

00:21:10.280 --> 00:21:12.900
It wasn't actually a windmill,

00:21:12.900 --> 00:21:15.120
but a wind station's turbine.

00:21:16.990 --> 00:21:19.440
I wasn't able to fly,

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:21.510
but the wind felt very nice.

00:21:24.270 --> 00:21:26.560
All right. I'll try and go next time.

00:21:27.730 --> 00:21:29.310
What are they talking about?

00:21:29.310 --> 00:21:31.930
Why do they seem so close 
all of a sudden?

00:21:32.540 --> 00:21:33.510
Well, then.

00:21:37.640 --> 00:21:41.580
Miss Sasako, the house blend 
and Earl Grey are ready.

00:21:41.580 --> 00:21:42.900
Oh, right.

00:21:44.450 --> 00:21:46.030
Thank you for all of your hard work!

00:21:56.370 --> 00:21:59.500
I will attend.

00:23:54.990 --> 00:24:25.040
Next Time

00:23:58.130 --> 00:23:59.740
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.740 --> 00:24:01.000
What is it, Panda?

00:24:01.000 --> 00:24:04.290
Tell me some fancy word 
you know, Mr. Penguin.

00:24:04.290 --> 00:24:05.210
Canape.

00:24:05.210 --> 00:24:06.090
Women's work pants <i>(monpe)</i>?

00:24:06.090 --> 00:24:07.750
Not a pun <i>(dajare)</i>, 
he said fancy <i>(oshare)</i>.

00:24:07.750 --> 00:24:09.950
Mr. Penguin, don't we 
have to end this?

00:24:09.950 --> 00:24:10.780
Nope.

00:24:10.780 --> 00:24:13.480
I sort of want to keep 
talking for a while today.

00:24:13.480 --> 00:24:14.210
Let's end this.

00:24:14.210 --> 00:24:14.970
I knew it.

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:16.850
Next week on, Oh! Polar 
Bear's Café...

00:24:16.850 --> 00:24:18.620
You don't have to try 
so hard to change it.

00:24:18.620 --> 00:24:19.220
Let's end this.

00:24:19.220 --> 00:24:20.390
Oh! Enjoy!

00:24:20.390 --> 00:24:22.370
You're not gonna give up, 
are you, Miss Sasako?

00:24:21.670 --> 00:24:23.370
Polar Bear's Insomnia
Mr. Grizzly's First Love
